1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:03,010
(Love In Sync)

2
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:12,320
(Kim Myung Soo)

3
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:18,990
(Kang Min Ah)

4
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:41,880
(Love In Sync)

5
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:44,789
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

6
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:45,919
(in this drama are fictitious and unrelated to reality.)

7
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,120
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:49,320
After Shin Mi Jeong exposed Ji An's bullying,

9
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,730
her mother passed away not long after.

10
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:55,930
- Her mother? - She was already battling cancer.

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,170
It seems her mother was her only family.

12
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:00,100
It's a shame, especially at her young age.

13
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,640
Anyway, she's been a recluse ever since.

14
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,040
There's no record of her whereabouts.

15
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,910
And her place of residence is unclear.

16
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:08,510
Really?

17
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,380
But who do you think you're talking to?

18
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:13,280
I went to the hospital where her mother was admitted,

19
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,350
and told them to contact me if Mi Jeong shows up.

20
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:17,890
So let's just wait.

21
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:20,260
They said her mother's things were still there.

22
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,660
She wouldn't just throw away her mom's keepsakes, right?

23
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:33,770
You're back?

24
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:35,670
Yes.

25
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,439
- Where's Ha Yul? - She's asleep.

26
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,509
Sorry, Song Hwan.

27
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:42,540
I haven't been much help lately, have I?

28
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,880
It's fine. It'll be over soon anyway.

29
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,480
Get some rest.

30
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:50,550
Oh, right.

31
00:01:51,290 --> 00:01:52,290
You got some mail.

32
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:04,669
(Korea Psychological Counselling Association)

33
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:07,200
(Notice of Nullification of Disciplinary Action)

34
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,360
Is she cold?

35
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:44,110
What? Why are you glaring at me? Why?

36
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,340
I wasn't glaring.

37
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,880
Hey, I was just looking.

38
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,110
Then why were you looking at me?

39
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:53,650
It was creepy.

40
00:02:54,150 --> 00:02:55,220
Jeez.

41
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:00,890
Here.

42
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,120
Is this your first winter shoot?

43
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:05,460
You should be prepared for things like this.

44
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,300
You were just as unprepared when you were an idol.

45
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,850
It's...

46
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,120
Sorry.

47
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,050
What?

48
00:03:31,290 --> 00:03:32,290
I...

49
00:03:34,090 --> 00:03:35,460
I said I'm sorry.

50
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:38,430
For what?

51
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:40,090
Just, you know...

52
00:03:42,230 --> 00:03:43,770
For everything.

53
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:48,140
Are you sick or something?

54
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,040
You're unbelievable.

55
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,440
Anyway, I apologised.

56
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:07,790
Hello.

57
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:13,290
This is Mi Jeong, right?

58
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:14,860
Where are you right now?

59
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,569
This is the scene where your anger toward each other...

60
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:18,570
reaches its peak.

61
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:21,570
It's one of the most pivotal scenes in the story,

62
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,500
so I need you both to really focus.

63
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:26,969
- Yes. - But your chemistry is fantastic,

64
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:28,440
so I'm not worried about that, right?

65
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:35,020
All right. Let's take a short break, and then we'll start filming.

66
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,920
- Okay. - Okay.

67
00:04:58,540 --> 00:04:59,540
Here.

68
00:05:05,350 --> 00:05:06,350
Are you nervous?

69
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:09,680
Of course. It's the highlight of the movie.

70
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,860
And it's my first major scene with Yi Jin.

71
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,620
She's a great actress, you know.

72
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,730
It would be embarrassing if I'm the only one who bombs.

73
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:25,599
Are you feeling okay?

74
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,100
You seemed to have a cold this morning.

75
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,070
That's why I said you should go to the doctor.

76
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,769
What if I get drowsy from the medicine...

77
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:35,340
- right before a shoot? - You're a real pro now.

78
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:39,250
I was always a pro. It's just that no one noticed.

79
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:50,260
One moment.

80
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,760
Yes, Detective.

81
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:55,830
Yes.

82
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:58,030
Shin Mi Jeong?

83
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,440
Yes, I understand. I'll head over right now.

84
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,100
Okay, thank you.

85
00:06:05,710 --> 00:06:07,170
What's so serious?

86
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:10,410
I heard that Shin Mi Jeong showed up at the hospital.

87
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:11,880
Mi Jeong?

88
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:13,650
I think I have to go right now.

89
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,880
Right now? But the shoot is about to start.

90
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:17,720
This is a really important scene.

91
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:20,250
Don't worry. It's not far from here.

92
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:21,890
I'll be back soon.

93
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:26,230
Even if I'm late, now...

94
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:29,260
you'll be able to do it on your own.

95
00:06:30,570 --> 00:06:33,230
- What? - Believe in yourself.

96
00:06:49,350 --> 00:06:53,220
(132 Ga 4819)

97
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,410
Why isn't he coming even now?

98
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:23,120
All right, let's start shooting. Everyone on standby.

99
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:30,090
You're always so cruel, Detective.

100
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:34,230
- What? - I've heard a lot about you.

101
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,460
And how you conduct your investigations.

102
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:38,670
Like a game...

103
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:41,000
I heard you treated your cases like a game.

104
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,369
You solve them, but you miss what's important.

105
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:45,740
And you did it again, didn't you?

106
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:47,710
You said I knew everything.

107
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,380
You said I was the mastermind of this game.

108
00:07:50,650 --> 00:07:51,650
You're wrong.

109
00:07:52,350 --> 00:07:54,220
Everything you assumed was wrong.

110
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,100
You...

111
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,870
You knew exactly what Lim Jun Ho did.

112
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:16,340
And you played all of us to cover for him.

113
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:19,039
Because I was arrogant enough to think I had figured out...

114
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,380
about you, the people I care about got hurt.

115
00:08:24,150 --> 00:08:26,309
If you think you're the only one who's suffered through all this,

116
00:08:26,310 --> 00:08:27,310
you're sorely mistaken.

117
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:31,520
That's why I'm going to solve this, no matter what.

118
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:35,590
Even if it means I have to take a completely different approach.

119
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,460
Cut, okay.

120
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:44,630
Are you awake?

121
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,760
You should have told me you had such a high fever.

122
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,400
Excuse me, the patient here...

123
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Don't go.

124
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:58,840
Don't go.

125
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:03,210
I said don't go.

126
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,900
- Why are you calling? - Hey, I found him.

127
00:10:25,570 --> 00:10:26,930
I found Kim Min Su.

128
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,439
(Scene 31, Hospital Hall, Night, Jeong Min Standing with a Phone)

129
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,639
He's overseas right now,

130
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,040
so he said he didn't know about Ji An's situation.

131
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:36,210
If you look at the original script he gave me,

132
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,710
the lines are identical to Ji An's bullying video.

133
00:10:44,490 --> 00:10:45,649
He also said...

134
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:48,820
that he had the screen test footage for Ji An's part.

135
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,060
He said he'd send it over no matter how long it takes if we want.

136
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,760
He must have been secretly grateful to Ji An.

137
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,500
Well, he was an unknown director, but she didn't ignore him,

138
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,170
and agreed to be in his movie.

139
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:03,270
So, if we get the original script and the screen test footage,

140
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:06,810
won't that clear Ji An of the false bullying accusation right away?

141
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:11,180
And if we find out who was behind this,

142
00:11:12,950 --> 00:11:13,950
it'll all be over.

143
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:20,550
(Detective)

144
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:36,940
Do Hoon, hold on.

145
00:11:37,910 --> 00:11:38,910
This is Yi Jin's...

146
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:43,480
Why doesn't he ever listen?

147
00:11:51,690 --> 00:11:52,690
Mr. Cha.

148
00:11:53,450 --> 00:11:57,260
So I checked Shin Mi Jeong's bank records just in case,

149
00:11:57,990 --> 00:11:59,129
and I found out a large sum of money was deposited...

150
00:11:59,130 --> 00:12:00,530
right before the scandal broke.

151
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,000
The depositor was Han Yi Jin.

152
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:10,300
Why would Yi Jin send her so much money?

153
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,540
I think...

154
00:12:16,310 --> 00:12:17,580
I think there's another culprit.

155
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:19,780
Is that really true?

156
00:12:20,050 --> 00:12:21,279
Are you sure Yi Jin has been in contact...

157
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:22,950
with Shin Mi Jeong?

158
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:24,950
Well, I don't know if they're in contact,

159
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:26,590
but I saw her on the phone with her a few times.

160
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:29,489
On top of that, Yi Jin was the one...

161
00:12:29,490 --> 00:12:32,690
who connected Ji An to that thug, CEO Noh.

162
00:12:33,730 --> 00:12:34,760
If you think about it,

163
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:37,230
Yi Jin is a more likely suspect than the CEO, isn't she?

164
00:12:37,970 --> 00:12:39,430
They've been enemies from the start.

165
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,670
- That's why the bullying video... - Is that really true?

166
00:12:46,210 --> 00:12:47,940
Did Yi Jin really do that to me?

167
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,280
Ji An.

168
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,720
Ji An.

169
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:08,360
(Actress Han Yi Jin's Dressing Room)

170
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:11,230
Ji An.

171
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:23,080
We were in the middle of shooting a vlog.

172
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:33,650
Gosh, now there's even an assault on set.

173
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,519
I've been in this business for a long time,

174
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,760
but this is a first. What are you going to do now?

175
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:43,999
Hey, someone else did the hitting,

176
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,400
so why are you blaming the innocent Director Moon?

177
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,269
I was so against it, but he insisted on casting her.

178
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:51,010
He has to take responsibility.

179
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:53,710
How should I take responsibility?

180
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:57,280
Fire Yu Ji An.

181
00:13:57,680 --> 00:14:00,649
Wait, if we fire Yu Ji An now,

182
00:14:00,650 --> 00:14:02,320
what about the production costs for what we've already filmed?

183
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,920
That's not my problem.

184
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:07,349
How can the attacker and the victim act in the same space?

185
00:14:07,350 --> 00:14:08,920
This is secondary victimization.

186
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:12,159
CEO Kim, please. Let's all calm down first.

187
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,760
CEO Kim does have a point.

188
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,270
I also feel that what happened on my set...

189
00:14:19,570 --> 00:14:20,930
was deeply regrettable.

190
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,740
For now, let's suspend Yu Ji An's filming.

191
00:14:27,110 --> 00:14:29,840
We'll figure out the next steps as we go.

192
00:14:31,810 --> 00:14:32,880
Director Moon.

193
00:14:33,510 --> 00:14:36,120
Come on, Director Moon, don't be too enraged.

194
00:14:41,690 --> 00:14:43,389
Filming people to back them into a corner...

195
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:44,460
must be your hobby.

196
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:47,230
But what a shame.

197
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:50,299
I don't think you'll be able to enjoy...

198
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:52,230
that little hobby of yours anymore.

199
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:56,170
Because I'm going to make sure to block you.

200
00:15:12,890 --> 00:15:15,060
Since there's no filming for a while anyway,

201
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,060
you don't have to come in starting tomorrow.

202
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:20,359
No, scratch that. Since it looks like...

203
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,730
I won't be able to make a comeback,

204
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,670
why don't we just terminate our contract?

205
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,600
That's what you wanted, right?

206
00:15:32,710 --> 00:15:33,710
Then, goodbye.

207
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,150
I told you to leave. Why are you still standing there?

208
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,090
I said go. Go.

209
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:50,260
You were so desperate to leave.

210
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,690
- Ji An... - Just get out.

211
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,300
What did I do?

212
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:00,600
What did I do that was so wrong?

213
00:16:02,970 --> 00:16:05,640
Why is everyone so eager to leave me?

214
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:10,140
People, CEO Kim,

215
00:16:11,510 --> 00:16:12,550
Mi Jeong,

216
00:16:13,710 --> 00:16:14,820
and Yi Jin.

217
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:16,920
Why?

218
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,920
Why?

219
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:24,590
You're just going to abandon me in the end anyway.

220
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:26,660
So...

221
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,760
just get out of here now.

222
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,640
When you're hurting like this,

223
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:39,310
how could I possibly leave?

224
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,220
So don't leave.

225
00:16:57,020 --> 00:17:01,060
Don't abandon me, Cha Eun Hwan.

226
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,500
Please.

227
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:45,870
I told you, didn't I?

228
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:49,310
That I'd make sure you make a successful comeback.

229
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:52,310
Just trust me and wait a little longer.

230
00:17:52,710 --> 00:17:54,110
And make sure you eat.

231
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,750
He's really terrible at cooking.

232
00:18:58,710 --> 00:19:00,450
(Phone)

233
00:19:00,550 --> 00:19:02,420
(Mom)

234
00:19:05,350 --> 00:19:09,490
(Mom)

235
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:22,670
(My Daughter)

236
00:19:28,210 --> 00:19:29,379
The party you are trying to reach is unavailable.

237
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:30,880
You will be connected to their voicemail...

238
00:19:40,890 --> 00:19:41,890
(The Late Park Yoon Hee)

239
00:19:41,891 --> 00:19:43,020
(Born: October 17, 1972, Died: January 24, 2026)

240
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:51,570
Who are you?

241
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,740
Ms. Shin Mi Jeong?

242
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:02,979
I came because I thought you might be here...

243
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:04,140
for your mother's memorial.

244
00:20:04,810 --> 00:20:07,510
- I'm glad I found you. - Who are you?

245
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:09,720
I'm Yu Ji An's manager.

246
00:20:14,150 --> 00:20:17,360
First, I'm very sorry for your loss.

247
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:20,360
You must have been through so much.

248
00:20:21,730 --> 00:20:25,830
I know exactly why you're here, but it's no use.

249
00:20:26,770 --> 00:20:29,000
I don't want to get involved in that case anymore.

250
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:33,070
Call me selfish and awful, but there's nothing I can do.

251
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:36,680
As for clearing Ji An of the bullying accusation,

252
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:39,950
I already have enough evidence to do that.

253
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:43,250
It's just that...

254
00:20:45,690 --> 00:20:47,690
the reason I came to find you, Mi Jeong,

255
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:51,760
was in the hope of sparing Ji An some pain.

256
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:55,200
That's all.

257
00:20:57,630 --> 00:20:58,630
Ji An...

258
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:01,500
Is she having a hard time?

259
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:05,440
Being betrayed by someone you trusted...

260
00:21:06,010 --> 00:21:07,840
is a pretty terrible thing.

261
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,410
I'm not going to force you.

262
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:14,480
The choice is yours to make.

263
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,120
I'll be on my way, then.

264
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:19,450
Wait.

265
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:23,120
He said he'd introduce me to a doctor who could save my mom.

266
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:25,430
CEO Kim said that.

267
00:21:27,430 --> 00:21:29,160
I didn't betray her for money.

268
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:31,670
I really didn't.

269
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:42,940
Darn it.

270
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:45,349
Filming people to back them into a corner...

271
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:46,350
must be your hobby.

272
00:21:47,050 --> 00:21:48,649
I don't think you'll be able to enjoy...

273
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:50,450
that little hobby of yours anymore.

274
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:54,350
Fine.

275
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,290
The best defence is a good offence.

276
00:22:02,230 --> 00:22:03,299
Hey, Manager Kim.

277
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,900
Get the reporters together right now.

278
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:08,540
Stop arguing and just do what I told you.

279
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:13,240
(J.An Entertainment)

280
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:16,940
The CEO is about to leave for a press conference right now.

281
00:22:18,650 --> 00:22:19,679
I think he's planning...

282
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:21,580
to completely frame Ji An for assault.

283
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:23,420
Don't worry.

284
00:22:23,820 --> 00:22:26,490
Soon, nobody will believe a word that guy says.

285
00:22:33,690 --> 00:22:36,400
Fortunately, I'm only going to take down one guy.

286
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:40,500
So I'll give you a chance to save your own skin, Reporter Han.

287
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:45,910
This is the only piece of dirt I have on CEO Kim,

288
00:22:46,770 --> 00:22:47,870
but you, Reporter Han...

289
00:22:50,110 --> 00:22:51,510
I'm guessing it's a different story for you.

290
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:00,450
He needs to feel how gut-wrenching betrayal is...

291
00:23:01,290 --> 00:23:02,460
for himself.

292
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:09,959
(J.An Entertainment)

293
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:11,630
Is everyone here? What about Yi Jin?

294
00:23:13,730 --> 00:23:15,739
Darn it. She needs to be here...

295
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:18,770
and play the victim for this to be perfect.

296
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:22,180
Apparently, a lot more reporters showed up than we expected.

297
00:23:22,410 --> 00:23:24,779
Really? I guess she still has pull.

298
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:26,380
Even after hitting rock bottom, Yu Ji An still has clout.

299
00:23:28,050 --> 00:23:29,050
Let's go.

300
00:23:33,850 --> 00:23:35,959
What is this? Hey, CEO Won, what is it?

301
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:37,020
I'm busy right now...

302
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:41,830
What?

303
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:44,430
Reporter Han? What's that bastard up to?

304
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:46,100
Hey. Hold on.

305
00:23:50,170 --> 00:23:51,499
("Yu Ji An's Abuse of Power Controversy...")

306
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:52,839
("Was A Scheme by the CEO of J.An Entertainment")

307
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:53,970
Darn it.

308
00:23:59,050 --> 00:24:00,079
(A Confession)

309
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,080
(Revealing the Truth Behind the Yu Ji An's Bullying Case)

310
00:24:01,720 --> 00:24:04,249
No matter what I say, or for what reason,

311
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:06,049
I don't believe there are any excuses...

312
00:24:06,050 --> 00:24:07,790
for what I've done.

313
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:12,390
I will humbly accept the consequences for my actions.

314
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:15,930
Is your head just for decoration? You should try thinking for once...

315
00:24:18,770 --> 00:24:20,600
Am I being too calm to act like someone who's angry?

316
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:23,739
Is your head just for decoration?

317
00:24:23,740 --> 00:24:25,370
You should try thinking for once...

318
00:24:25,710 --> 00:24:27,670
Oh? Hey, perfect timing.

319
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:29,540
Again?

320
00:24:29,710 --> 00:24:32,179
You know, having someone to act with versus not,

321
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:33,410
makes a difference getting in character.

322
00:24:34,150 --> 00:24:35,879
Don't half-heartedly do it like before.

323
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:37,920
Act like you're really the one getting yelled at.

324
00:24:38,050 --> 00:24:39,320
That's how I can immerse myself in the role.

325
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:45,160
Hey, where is your head at?

326
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:46,860
How many times do I have to tell you?

327
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:50,700
Is your head just for decoration? Do you even think at all?

328
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:53,400
You have no idea what's going on, do you?

329
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:57,370
Gosh. You're really driving me crazy.

330
00:24:57,670 --> 00:24:59,970
What is all this mess just because of one bad hire?

331
00:25:00,870 --> 00:25:04,110
Hey, I'm just asking because I'm genuinely curious,

332
00:25:04,410 --> 00:25:06,210
do your parents know you go around acting like this?

333
00:25:08,210 --> 00:25:11,420
Oh my, look at her. Are you crying?

334
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:15,120
Hey, why are you crying? I said, why are you crying?

335
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:17,690
Who do you think should be the one crying right now?

336
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:21,430
I told you not to cry. Stop crying.

337
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:29,470
Hey, wasn't my acting amazing?

338
00:25:30,140 --> 00:25:32,540
Wasn't that just total method acting?

339
00:25:32,870 --> 00:25:37,740
I know. You're really good at acting angry.

340
00:25:38,910 --> 00:25:41,550
Who says you can't act? You're so good...

341
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:46,250
You act so good.

342
00:25:47,050 --> 00:25:48,520
You got the angles right, didn't you?

343
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:53,190
- Bring it here so I can watch it. - Okay.

344
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:56,930
Lastly,

345
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,799
I want to say I'm sorry to Ji An,

346
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:01,400
who was always so genuinely kind to me.

347
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:03,440
Ji An.

348
00:26:04,470 --> 00:26:05,840
I'm truly sorry.

349
00:26:12,710 --> 00:26:14,650
I knew it. I believed in her all along.

350
00:26:14,810 --> 00:26:16,779
She's amazing for enduring all that. All the best.

351
00:26:16,780 --> 00:26:19,319
It's so sad to think of all the hate she got.

352
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:23,020
- Wish you all the best from now on. - I'm glad the truth is finally out.

353
00:26:23,260 --> 00:26:26,730
She's a good actress too. Looks like she only has success ahead of her.

354
00:26:29,730 --> 00:26:30,730
I told you, didn't I?

355
00:26:31,730 --> 00:26:33,200
That you, Ji An, are absolutely...

356
00:26:35,370 --> 00:26:36,770
not that kind of person.

357
00:26:37,170 --> 00:26:39,070
So it really wasn't me.

358
00:26:40,170 --> 00:26:41,170
I...

359
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:44,880
I was afraid that I might really be that kind of awful person.

360
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,280
Thank you.

361
00:26:51,150 --> 00:26:52,150
For believing in me.

362
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,490
For revealing the truth.

363
00:26:59,130 --> 00:27:00,160
If you're that grateful,

364
00:27:01,930 --> 00:27:05,030
will you grant me a wish?

365
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:12,210
Is this really your wish? To spend the whole day with me?

366
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:16,680
Well, I never specified that it had to be you, Ji An.

367
00:27:17,710 --> 00:27:19,550
Just like how other people hang out with their friends,

368
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:22,179
I said I wanted to spend just one day...

369
00:27:22,180 --> 00:27:24,250
having fun without any worries.

370
00:27:26,090 --> 00:27:29,560
Because I've never been able to do that.

371
00:27:30,060 --> 00:27:31,060
Geez.

372
00:27:32,030 --> 00:27:36,330
If you want to go on a date with me, just be honest and say it.

373
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:39,730
How many times do I have to tell you that you can't hide it?

374
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:42,840
Are you dumb?

375
00:27:44,340 --> 00:27:45,340
I can hear everything, you know.

376
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,210
I can feel everything, you know.

377
00:27:53,510 --> 00:27:55,350
Friends hold hands when they hang out these days.

378
00:27:56,050 --> 00:27:57,050
Didn't you know?

379
00:28:19,710 --> 00:28:20,770
It's okay.

380
00:28:33,690 --> 00:28:35,050
It's...

381
00:28:56,810 --> 00:28:58,610
- This or that? - That one.

382
00:29:08,290 --> 00:29:09,690
Oh, they are cherry blossoms.

383
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,589
I've never been able to properly see...

384
00:29:11,590 --> 00:29:12,890
the cherry blossoms because of filming.

385
00:29:20,630 --> 00:29:21,630
Right now,

386
00:29:22,870 --> 00:29:25,070
I'm about to do the most selfish thing in my life.

387
00:29:27,070 --> 00:29:28,610
But just this once,

388
00:29:30,180 --> 00:29:31,410
will you look the other way?

389
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:37,280
You're here.

390
00:30:39,710 --> 00:30:41,780
- What are you doing here? - What do you mean?

391
00:30:42,150 --> 00:30:43,920
Starting today, I'm your manager.

392
00:30:44,780 --> 00:30:47,589
- What? - Didn't you hear anything...

393
00:30:47,590 --> 00:30:48,650
from Mr. Cha?

394
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,990
He came to me himself and asked me to take good care of you.

395
00:30:53,930 --> 00:30:55,830
- He said he's quitting. - He's quitting?

396
00:31:01,470 --> 00:31:05,540
The phone is turned off. Connecting to voicemail. After the beep...

397
00:31:06,940 --> 00:31:07,940
Where are you going?

398
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,090
Where's Eun Hwan?

399
00:31:24,460 --> 00:31:26,690
- He's home, right? - He's not here.

400
00:31:27,960 --> 00:31:32,530
- He left early this morning. - Left? Where to?

401
00:31:32,930 --> 00:31:34,300
He didn't say anything to me.

402
00:31:34,670 --> 00:31:35,670
I wouldn't know.

403
00:31:36,670 --> 00:31:38,570
He left without telling me anything specific either.

404
00:31:41,370 --> 00:31:44,580
But he must have had his reasons for leaving like that.

405
00:31:46,210 --> 00:31:47,280
Reasons?

406
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:50,850
- What... - Since they can never be together,

407
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:54,950
wouldn't being together be more like a punishment for them?

408
00:31:55,590 --> 00:31:59,960
Right now, I'm about to do the most selfish thing in my life.

409
00:32:19,750 --> 00:32:22,520
Unable to connect. You will be forwarded to voicemail.

410
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:30,560
Ji An, the interview is starting soon.

411
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:32,390
He hasn't contacted you either, right?

412
00:32:32,890 --> 00:32:33,890
Mr. Cha?

413
00:32:35,190 --> 00:32:36,200
No.

414
00:32:36,430 --> 00:32:38,330
Ever since he suddenly came to me and asked me to take care of you,

415
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:40,600
I haven't been able to contact him either.

416
00:32:49,110 --> 00:32:51,039
You must have had a very difficult time...

417
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:52,950
with the abuse of power controversy.

418
00:32:53,450 --> 00:32:57,050
Weren't you upset with the public for being so quick to judge?

419
00:32:58,850 --> 00:32:59,850
I understand.

420
00:33:00,590 --> 00:33:01,590
Even I...

421
00:33:02,820 --> 00:33:04,720
found it hard to believe in myself.

422
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:07,790
I'm not sure.

423
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:10,730
He didn't really say anything to me before he left either.

424
00:33:11,260 --> 00:33:13,800
You don't really expect me to believe that, do you?

425
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:16,369
There's no way he'd leave his sister and Ha Yul...

426
00:33:16,370 --> 00:33:17,670
without asking you for help.

427
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:21,310
Tell me everything you know. Where is he now?

428
00:33:21,770 --> 00:33:22,940
Why is he suddenly acting like this?

429
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:28,480
- Is he mad at me about something? - No.

430
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:29,979
It's not that.

431
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:31,980
Then what is it? Please, just tell me.

432
00:33:33,190 --> 00:33:34,550
I don't really know either.

433
00:33:34,650 --> 00:33:36,990
It just seems he has some things he needs to sort out.

434
00:33:39,430 --> 00:33:42,260
Sort out what?

435
00:34:06,190 --> 00:34:07,949
- Hello. - Hey, man.

436
00:34:07,950 --> 00:34:09,590
Thanks to you, there's no way I'm getting into heaven.

437
00:34:10,389 --> 00:34:12,060
How long do I have to play the bad guy?

438
00:34:12,560 --> 00:34:14,360
Do you have any idea how Ji An is doing right now?

439
00:34:15,929 --> 00:34:17,030
Is she having a hard time?

440
00:34:17,429 --> 00:34:18,429
Of course she is.

441
00:34:18,699 --> 00:34:20,468
The person she likes vanished into thin air.

442
00:34:20,469 --> 00:34:21,630
How could she possibly be okay?

443
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:26,639
Man, she's a complete wreck. I was worried she'd collapse.

444
00:34:27,909 --> 00:34:28,909
And you...

445
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:30,480
Are you okay?

446
00:34:31,010 --> 00:34:32,080
I'm fine.

447
00:34:32,750 --> 00:34:34,210
You're the one going through a hard time because of me.

448
00:34:36,650 --> 00:34:37,650
Sorry.

449
00:34:38,219 --> 00:34:39,820
He always says he's fine.

450
00:34:40,389 --> 00:34:42,360
I must be crazy for even asking.

451
00:34:43,060 --> 00:34:44,060
Hey, you too, man.

452
00:34:44,790 --> 00:34:45,989
Don't suffer for too long before you come back.

453
00:34:46,630 --> 00:34:47,630
I'll make you a meal.

454
00:34:48,730 --> 00:34:49,730
I'm hanging up.

455
00:35:17,860 --> 00:35:21,060
Unable to connect. You will be forwarded to voicemail.

456
00:35:23,260 --> 00:35:24,730
What is the reason for all this?

457
00:35:25,130 --> 00:35:27,200
Shouldn't you at least give me a reason?

458
00:35:27,700 --> 00:35:30,340
Eun Hwan, were you always this selfish and irresponsible?

459
00:35:33,010 --> 00:35:35,910
Forget it. From now on, wherever you are,

460
00:35:37,410 --> 00:35:39,110
I don't care what you do.

461
00:35:40,380 --> 00:35:41,550
So don't ever contact me again.

462
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:44,880
Your message has been saved.

463
00:35:46,990 --> 00:35:48,620
Did you go on a trip somewhere?

464
00:35:49,460 --> 00:35:51,260
It must be a really great place...

465
00:35:51,860 --> 00:35:53,160
if you left without a word to me.

466
00:35:55,130 --> 00:35:56,130
You should have taken me with you.

467
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:58,160
That's so cheap.

468
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,270
Can't you at least call me?

469
00:36:02,500 --> 00:36:03,540
I'm so...

470
00:36:06,710 --> 00:36:08,210
I'm so worried.

471
00:36:09,980 --> 00:36:12,480
Cha Eun Hwan, you're...

472
00:36:13,750 --> 00:36:16,180
You're such a jerk. A complete jerk.

473
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:23,620
Fine, have a great life all by yourself.

474
00:36:24,590 --> 00:36:25,590
Just you wait until you get back.

475
00:36:26,390 --> 00:36:28,160
I won't let you get away with this.

476
00:36:29,230 --> 00:36:30,230
Next message.

477
00:36:31,600 --> 00:36:32,830
When you come back,

478
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,370
I'll forgive you for everything.

479
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,670
So, please just come back.

480
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:40,610
I miss you so much.

481
00:36:41,940 --> 00:36:44,610
No more messages.

482
00:36:55,220 --> 00:36:56,489
(Dong Gyeong Kitchen)

483
00:36:56,490 --> 00:36:57,490
Welcome.

484
00:36:59,090 --> 00:37:01,330
Have you heard from him?

485
00:37:02,860 --> 00:37:03,860
No.

486
00:37:20,110 --> 00:37:22,720
Here's your order. Enjoy.

487
00:37:27,290 --> 00:37:28,290
Still nothing?

488
00:37:29,260 --> 00:37:30,390
Yes, well...

489
00:37:38,730 --> 00:37:41,630
This is driving me crazy.

490
00:37:44,640 --> 00:37:45,640
Yes, we're closed now.

491
00:37:48,970 --> 00:37:49,980
Still...

492
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,170
You have soju here, right?

493
00:38:13,570 --> 00:38:14,570
Soju?

494
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:16,170
You mean, not sparkling water?

495
00:39:04,480 --> 00:39:06,820
Hey. Come on out, Cha Eun Hwan.

496
00:39:07,390 --> 00:39:09,360
You jerk. You're in there, aren't you?

497
00:39:10,090 --> 00:39:11,090
You selfish jerk.

498
00:39:11,690 --> 00:39:13,130
You think I can't find you?

499
00:39:13,660 --> 00:39:16,700
You jerk, I said come out. Come out.

500
00:39:27,770 --> 00:39:28,770
You jerk.

501
00:39:29,780 --> 00:39:32,110
Are you having fun toying with my heart?

502
00:39:36,780 --> 00:39:38,950
I passed. I got the part.

503
00:39:40,750 --> 00:39:43,959
One, two, three.

504
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,690
Friends hold hands when they hang out these days.

505
00:39:53,700 --> 00:39:55,300
You shouldn't have been so nice to me.

506
00:39:57,640 --> 00:39:58,900
You shouldn't have made me fall for you.

507
00:40:00,810 --> 00:40:02,170
If you were just going to disappear like this,

508
00:40:03,940 --> 00:40:05,340
what am I supposed to do?

509
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:19,689
Ladies and gentlemen,

510
00:40:19,690 --> 00:40:21,129
our plane will be arriving...

511
00:40:21,130 --> 00:40:23,499
at Incheon International Airport shortly.

512
00:40:23,500 --> 00:40:25,499
Please be seated and ensure your seatbelts...

513
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:28,770
are securely fastened. Thank you.

514
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:38,310
Watch out.

515
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:41,980
Ji An.

516
00:40:48,490 --> 00:40:50,489
Where are you right now? Ji An got hurt,

517
00:40:50,490 --> 00:40:51,720
and she's asking for you.

518
00:40:57,800 --> 00:41:04,440
(Regional Emergency Medical Center)

519
00:41:08,070 --> 00:41:10,379
I'm here. Where should I go? How is Ji An...

520
00:41:10,380 --> 00:41:14,080
I'm sorry. I had no other choice.

521
00:41:28,260 --> 00:41:29,290
Your injuries...

522
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:31,500
Are you okay?

523
00:41:34,670 --> 00:41:36,270
You jerk.

524
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:53,120
Did you have a nice trip?

525
00:41:54,920 --> 00:41:55,920
You're not angry?

526
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:58,020
I can tell...

527
00:41:58,690 --> 00:42:00,060
how sorry you are.

528
00:42:01,530 --> 00:42:02,530
Then...

529
00:42:02,860 --> 00:42:04,560
why did you do something you'd feel so sorry about?

530
00:42:07,900 --> 00:42:09,000
Are you...

531
00:42:09,900 --> 00:42:11,400
upset with me about something?

532
00:42:15,710 --> 00:42:16,740
Or...

533
00:42:17,780 --> 00:42:19,340
did I do something wrong?

534
00:42:20,380 --> 00:42:21,380
No.

535
00:42:22,080 --> 00:42:23,150
It's not that.

536
00:42:30,660 --> 00:42:31,720
It's just that...

537
00:42:33,030 --> 00:42:34,360
I've been having a hard time.

538
00:42:37,430 --> 00:42:38,830
I mean, from my perspective,

539
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:41,230
helping you with your comeback,

540
00:42:41,830 --> 00:42:44,470
playing manager, which I'm not cut out for,

541
00:42:44,670 --> 00:42:45,940
and channelling your emotions...

542
00:42:47,170 --> 00:42:48,410
Of course it wasn't going to be easy.

543
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:51,140
So you were cleared of the bullying accusation.

544
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:53,810
And since you started acting well without me,

545
00:42:54,450 --> 00:42:55,910
I thought it was the right time to leave.

546
00:42:56,750 --> 00:42:57,980
If that was too sudden,

547
00:42:59,420 --> 00:43:00,450
I'm sorry about that.

548
00:43:01,950 --> 00:43:02,960
All that time...

549
00:43:05,260 --> 00:43:07,530
Was being with me...

550
00:43:09,830 --> 00:43:10,930
that difficult for you?

551
00:43:20,410 --> 00:43:21,440
I see.

552
00:43:24,580 --> 00:43:25,840
But I enjoyed our time together.

553
00:43:31,250 --> 00:43:32,250
So...

554
00:43:32,750 --> 00:43:34,490
Did you enjoy your trip?

555
00:43:35,120 --> 00:43:36,290
Where did you go?

556
00:43:36,920 --> 00:43:39,220
The beach? The mountains?

557
00:43:41,130 --> 00:43:42,160
Just...

558
00:43:43,600 --> 00:43:44,600
a fishing spot.

559
00:43:46,130 --> 00:43:47,170
A fishing spot?

560
00:43:48,130 --> 00:43:49,270
It's a place I often went to with my father...

561
00:43:51,270 --> 00:43:53,010
when I was a kid.

562
00:43:54,170 --> 00:43:55,770
I suddenly felt the urge to go there.

563
00:43:59,010 --> 00:44:00,050
That must have been nice.

564
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:04,980
So nice that you didn't even think of me.

565
00:44:06,820 --> 00:44:08,550
You could have at least reached out.

566
00:44:09,320 --> 00:44:12,590
- So I wouldn't have to worry. - What exactly are we?

567
00:44:14,160 --> 00:44:15,690
I'm not your manager anymore.

568
00:44:16,460 --> 00:44:17,599
We're not in any kind of relationship.

569
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:20,230
If a scandal breaks out because we're messaging each other...

570
00:44:21,570 --> 00:44:25,640
You have to be careful after your difficult comeback.

571
00:44:25,940 --> 00:44:27,310
Do you really think that?

572
00:44:28,670 --> 00:44:30,140
That we're nothing to each other?

573
00:44:41,790 --> 00:44:43,890
If we're nothing, then why are you here today?

574
00:44:44,620 --> 00:44:46,960
When you hear that someone who means nothing to you got hurt,

575
00:44:47,730 --> 00:44:49,600
do you always come running like a madman?

576
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:58,070
Even if it hadn't been you, Yu Ji An, I would've done the same.

577
00:44:58,540 --> 00:44:59,540
So,

578
00:45:00,040 --> 00:45:03,440
- don't read too much into it. - Then what was that kiss about?

579
00:45:06,680 --> 00:45:09,750
Does a kiss really mean that much between us?

580
00:45:12,850 --> 00:45:14,020
That kiss was...

581
00:45:14,320 --> 00:45:16,050
just my way of saying goodbye.

582
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:18,360
Are we clear?

583
00:45:20,230 --> 00:45:21,790
Then why can't you look me in the eye?

584
00:45:23,100 --> 00:45:25,460
It's because you don't want me to see how you feel, isn't it?

585
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:29,739
- That's... - Do you know what the...

586
00:45:29,740 --> 00:45:30,970
hardest part for me right now is?

587
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:34,310
The fact I know that every word you're saying...

588
00:45:35,970 --> 00:45:37,510
is a lie.

589
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:40,450
I know it all.

590
00:45:41,080 --> 00:45:42,350
And I can feel it all.

591
00:45:43,950 --> 00:45:45,980
So why are you so desperate to push me away?

592
00:45:46,390 --> 00:45:47,390
Why?

593
00:45:54,490 --> 00:45:56,160
You really don't know why?

594
00:45:58,700 --> 00:46:00,900
Someone who knows my every feeling.

595
00:46:03,240 --> 00:46:05,070
Don't you think that would be terrifying for me?

596
00:46:18,520 --> 00:46:20,120
I know you're lying.

597
00:46:45,880 --> 00:46:48,880
(JJ Actors Entertainment)

598
00:46:50,950 --> 00:46:52,219
(Cha Eun Hwan, Therapist, Tok Tok Mental Care)

599
00:46:52,220 --> 00:46:54,520
(Observation: Ji An is exhibiting considerably open emotions.)

600
00:46:55,320 --> 00:46:57,460
(CEO Kim)

601
00:47:04,300 --> 00:47:06,670
(Controversial Therapy Method: "Imaginary Revenge" Psychotherapy)

602
00:47:11,740 --> 00:47:13,840
(CEO Kim Jun Sik)

603
00:47:18,910 --> 00:47:19,949
The party you are trying to reach is unavailable.

604
00:47:19,950 --> 00:47:21,650
You will be connected to their voicemail...

605
00:47:24,020 --> 00:47:25,280
She's ignoring my calls?

606
00:47:26,350 --> 00:47:27,350
Darn it.

607
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:30,190
What, does she expect me to take the fall for this alone?

608
00:47:34,430 --> 00:47:35,430
CEO Kim.

609
00:47:35,730 --> 00:47:38,060
What? What is it?

610
00:47:38,930 --> 00:47:41,200
Two of the rookie actors we signed last month...

611
00:47:41,970 --> 00:47:43,440
have filed a lawsuit to terminate their contracts.

612
00:47:50,010 --> 00:47:51,680
Those pathetic little punks.

613
00:47:52,080 --> 00:47:53,080
And...

614
00:47:53,210 --> 00:47:54,210
(District Court)

615
00:47:54,410 --> 00:47:55,410
Han Yi Jin, too.

616
00:47:57,920 --> 00:47:58,920
What?

617
00:48:00,390 --> 00:48:01,390
Han Yi Jin?

618
00:48:06,090 --> 00:48:07,289
(Complaint)

619
00:48:07,290 --> 00:48:09,060
(Plaintiff: Han Yi Jin, Defendant: CEO Kim Jun Sik)

620
00:48:12,730 --> 00:48:14,030
(Suit to Confirm Exclusive Contract Termination)

621
00:48:15,230 --> 00:48:16,670
(CEO Kim Jun Sik)

622
00:48:16,970 --> 00:48:17,970
Darn it.

623
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:22,310
(For Sale)

624
00:48:22,970 --> 00:48:24,310
All right, great. Let's do it.

625
00:48:24,780 --> 00:48:26,509
Wait, you're really going to sign right now?

626
00:48:26,510 --> 00:48:27,979
You should look at a few more places.

627
00:48:27,980 --> 00:48:31,320
- The location isn't great. - But I have the skills.

628
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:33,050
So what's the worry?

629
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:35,649
Now that I hear you talk, I'm reminded...

630
00:48:35,650 --> 00:48:37,159
of what a jerk you've always been.

631
00:48:37,160 --> 00:48:39,359
(For Rent or Sale)

632
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:41,160
I want to start working as soon as possible.

633
00:48:41,730 --> 00:48:43,900
It'll keep my mind off things.

634
00:48:48,670 --> 00:48:49,670
What?

635
00:48:49,970 --> 00:48:52,500
The forecast didn't say anything about rain today.

636
00:48:56,340 --> 00:48:58,880
I can't breathe.

637
00:49:00,410 --> 00:49:02,250
Just do exactly as I do, okay?

638
00:49:03,350 --> 00:49:05,220
Breathe in. One, two.

639
00:49:06,380 --> 00:49:07,990
Breathe out. Three, four.

640
00:49:18,360 --> 00:49:19,870
I'm not your manager anymore.

641
00:49:20,830 --> 00:49:22,099
We're not in any kind of relationship.

642
00:49:22,100 --> 00:49:24,570
If a scandal breaks out because we're messaging each other...

643
00:49:28,040 --> 00:49:29,910
(Mom)

644
00:49:38,280 --> 00:49:41,649
(Mom)

645
00:49:41,650 --> 00:49:43,160
(Tuesday, March 24)

646
00:50:01,370 --> 00:50:04,379
Hello? Could you please open the door?

647
00:50:04,380 --> 00:50:05,910
Hello? Is anybody there?

648
00:50:07,280 --> 00:50:08,750
Please, open the door.

649
00:50:21,560 --> 00:50:22,560
Ji An.

650
00:50:22,930 --> 00:50:24,800
The shoot's cancelled because of the rain.

651
00:50:24,900 --> 00:50:27,230
(Actress Yu Ji An's Dressing Room)

652
00:50:27,630 --> 00:50:28,630
What the...

653
00:50:29,800 --> 00:50:30,840
Is it broken?

654
00:50:34,610 --> 00:50:35,610
Oh, man.

655
00:50:36,470 --> 00:50:38,810
It's raining out. This is so annoying.

656
00:50:39,880 --> 00:50:41,450
Ji An, are you in there?

657
00:50:42,650 --> 00:50:43,720
Ji An, are you okay?

658
00:50:45,780 --> 00:50:46,790
Ji An.

659
00:50:54,090 --> 00:50:55,090
Pick up.

660
00:50:56,360 --> 00:50:58,299
Yes, is this maintenance? The door here is broken.

661
00:50:58,300 --> 00:50:59,330
Please send someone quickly.

662
00:50:59,970 --> 00:51:01,300
Right now.

663
00:51:02,070 --> 00:51:03,500
Ji An is in there, and she is claustrophobic.

664
00:51:04,570 --> 00:51:05,870
Help me.

665
00:51:07,710 --> 00:51:08,970
Help me.

666
00:51:10,610 --> 00:51:11,910
Help me.

667
00:51:12,980 --> 00:51:14,150
Help me.

668
00:51:15,310 --> 00:51:19,080
Kiddo, if you don't want to do this, you can just say so.

669
00:51:19,420 --> 00:51:20,820
No one will be mad at you.

670
00:51:22,550 --> 00:51:24,990
You'll be all by yourself in this warehouse set.

671
00:51:25,490 --> 00:51:26,520
Aren't you scared?

672
00:51:28,960 --> 00:51:31,230
No. I'm not scared.

673
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:34,170
If at any point you get scared or feel like you're in danger,

674
00:51:34,430 --> 00:51:35,730
just scream for help.

675
00:51:36,170 --> 00:51:39,900
And I'll come running like Superman to save you.

676
00:51:40,240 --> 00:51:42,370
- Got it? - Okay.

677
00:51:43,880 --> 00:51:44,880
Okay.

678
00:51:48,880 --> 00:51:50,750
Kiddo, stay with me.

679
00:51:51,280 --> 00:51:52,280
Kiddo.

680
00:51:54,750 --> 00:51:55,950
Are you okay?

681
00:51:56,350 --> 00:51:57,520
Help me.

682
00:51:58,890 --> 00:52:00,060
Help me.

683
00:52:00,460 --> 00:52:03,700
Okay. I'll definitely save you.

684
00:52:06,100 --> 00:52:07,770
Don't lose consciousness, okay?
